note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note Contract section 4: two nested unroll 64 loops make 4096 copies of a 12-statement body of unsigned
note ops on run-time values (each statement at least two instructions, so at least 98304 words). Each
note loop alone is within the 64-copy bound. Through omc f4fa7951 the 65536-word bound of a function
note refused it (error 14, obligation=growth); since 2026-11-11 a function has no word bound (OMEGESE
note 9.6), so it compiles and gives exactly the rolled twin's output (unroll-growth-rolled).
note Twin unroll-growth-diag.om checks the om2 diag record.
om2
fn grow a ulong to ulong
x = a
s = add a 1
t = add a 2
u = add a 3
for i ulong 64 unroll
for j ulong 64 unroll
x = add mul x 3 add s add i j
s = xor s shr x 7
t = add t mul s x
u = xor u shl t 3
x = add x mul u 5
s = add s xor x t
t = xor t shr s 11
u = add u mul t 9
x = xor x add u s
s = mul s add x 1
t = add t xor u 13
u = xor u add s t
end
end
ret xor xor x s xor t u
end
fn main to int
ret int and grow 5 255
end
